  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nTo solve the equation $x/2 - 1/3 = 3x/4 + 5$:\n\n1.  Multiply every term by 12 (the least common multiple of 2, 3, and 4) to eliminate fractions:\n    $$12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) - 12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) = 12 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{3x}{4}\\right) + 12 \\cdot 5$$\n    $$6x - 4 = 9x + 60$$\n\n2.  Subtract $6x$ from both sides:\n    $$-4 = 3x + 60$$\n\n3.  Subtract 60 from both sides:\n    $$-64 = 3x$$\n\n4.  Divide by 3:\n    $$x = -\\frac{64}{3}$$"
